# OFF-BOX EXCLUSIONS — the suites the hermetic partition leaves out.
#
# FORMAT (frozen contract, copied from scripts/host-suites.manifest): plain text, one
# `tests/<name>.bats` per line, `#` comments and blank lines ignored. Consumer:
#   scripts/offbox-partition.sh   partition = tests/*.bats MINUS host-suites.manifest MINUS THIS
# The partition is a SET DIFFERENCE, so it is total by construction and never hand-synced: a NEW
# suite lands INSIDE the partition and must earn its way out with a line here and a reason.
#
# ── WHAT AN EXCLUSION COSTS HERE, AND WHY THE BAR IS LOWER THAN host-suites.manifest's ───────────
# Removing a suite from `host-suites.manifest` removes it from THE tree verdict and from the land
# smoke — that manifest's header records the bill exactly once: 151 tests excluded from both for a
# property not one of them had. THIS list cannot do that. The suites below still run in the on-box
# corpus, in `/ship`'s smoke, and in every existing gate, unchanged. All an entry here does is keep
# a suite out of a SECOND, ADDITIVE opinion that did not exist at all before 2026-08-10.
# So the bar is not "proven machine-coupled" — it is "does not yet produce a usable off-box signal".
# The direction of the mistake matters: an over-broad entry here loses coverage that never existed,
# while a missing entry stops the producer producing anything for everyone. Neither is free, and the
# census arm below is what keeps the first from becoming permanent.
#
# ── EVERY ENTRY IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A JUDGEMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seeded from the FIRST real off-box run — GitHub Actions run 31362043861, macos-latest, 2026-08-10,
# 306 suites executed: 279 green, 26 red, 1 cut. Each entry records the `notok` count that run
# observed. That is deliberately the whole justification: a cause ("this needs iTerm2") is a
# hypothesis, and this repo has paid for seeding an exclusion list from a conflated cause before.
# Where the subject makes the cause obvious it is named as a HINT and marked as one; nothing here
# claims a cause was verified.
#
# ── THE LIST IS RE-MEASURED, NOT CURATED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `scripts/offbox-run.sh census` runs EVERY suite, excluded ones included, so an entry that has
# started passing off-box shows up as passing and can be deleted. That is the upward half. The
# downward half is in `offbox-partition.sh lint`: a stale entry (no such suite) and an entry already
# granted by host-suites.manifest are both RED. Without the census arm this file would be an
# exemption list that only ever grows, which is precisely what a ratchet must never become.
#
# ── HOW TO DELETE A LINE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run the census, confirm the suite is green off-box, delete its line and its comment in one commit.
# Nothing else is needed: the partition widens by set difference on the next run.

